BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Voyage Hot Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270123T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270123T210000
UID:6af79d13f1f337004472ae82@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Django meets French Chanson\nAward-winning violinist\nEva Slon
 go\n\, guitarist\nJimmy Grant\nand Double bassist\nSimon Planting\npresent
  an intimate and swinging duo rooted in the gypsy jazz tradition of\nDjang
 o Reinhardt\nand\nStéphane Grappelli\n. Their music draws equally from Eu
 ropean jazz\, Eastern European folk influences\, and classic vocal jazz\, 
 resulting in a sound that feels both timeless and accessible to modern aud
 iences.\nTheir repertoire includes French chanson\, swing standards\, and 
 original arrangements that evoke travel\, nostalgia\, and joy. Whether pre
 sented in a listening-room jazz club\, concert hall\, or outdoor summer se
 ries\, Eva and Jimmy offer a warm\, dynamic performance that emphasizes gr
 oove\, melody\, and connection.\nTickets for this event are $33 GA\, $28 f
 or OCA members. Doors open at 6:30 PM\, refreshments available. Art Galler
 y open during intermission Contact us to request ADA seating\,\ninfo@occid
 entalcenterforthearts.org\nGet Tickets\nAbout the performers:\nJimmy Grant
 \,\nhailing from Northern California\, discovered Django Reinhardt's vibra
 nt sounds while touring with his dad’s bluegrass band. His unique style\
 , shaped by influences like Bach and Joe Pass\, was honed under the mentor
 ship of guitarists Jim Nichols and Howard Alden.\nJimmy has performed with
  renowned artists such as David Grisman\, Gonzalo Bergara\, and many more 
 showcasing his talent at prestigious events like Djangofest Northwest and 
 The New York Hot Jazz Festival\, as well as venues throughout the US & Eur
 ope.\nAs an educator\, he teaches across the U.S. and hosts "Camp Django" 
 in Ashland\, OR. He contributes to "Gypsy Jazz Secrets Magazine" and has r
 ecorded two albums. His original composition "Insomnia" was a finalist in 
 the John Lennon Songwriting Competition.\nEva Slongo\nwas born in Switzerl
 and to a family of classical musicians. She first trained as a professiona
 l classical violinist.\nOne day\, by chance\, she tried to improvise with 
 musicians in a bar\; she felt such euphoria that she spent a sleepless nig
 ht … It was then that she decided to do everything she could to practice
  improvisation on the violin.\nAfter her classical diplomas\, she changed 
 direction and started from scratch … She studied jazz violin with Pierre
  Blanchard in Lausanne\, then with Didier Lockwood in Paris\, where she de
 cided to stay and live for music. She also practiced improvisation on voca
 ls\, which led her to create her very noticeable unique color: improvising
  on the violin and scatting simultaneously.\nIn Paris\, Eva Slongo met ren
 owned musicians from the world of gypsy jazz with whom she shared the stag
 e: Biréli Lagrène\, Wawau Adler\, Sébastien Giniaux\, Ninine Garcia\, a
 nd many others …\nIn 2011\, she won the Prize for Best Improvisation at 
 the Stéphane Grappelli International Violin Competition sponsored by Didi
 er Lockwood. In 2016\, she obtained the 2nd prize of the Golden Jazz Troph
 y with her quartet.\nAfter all these years of experience\, she was led to 
 give masterclasses internationally. She needed to share more of her learni
 ng of the jazz violin\, but struggled to find the time and method to do so
 . Her first pregnancy forced her to slow down concerts… but it led her t
 o do what she would never have imagined: create a new educational concept 
 on the internet\, the blog “Learn Jazz Violin” which has become the 1s
 t Google search result in French jazz violin\, and finally a method “The
  new way to learn jazz violin.”\nEva Slongo’s new album “Souffle” 
 was recorded in collaboration with pianist Giovanni Mirabassi\, with whom 
 she shares the stage regularly.\nDutch double bassist\nSimon Planting\nstu
 died classical bass at the Royal Concertgebouw Orchestra and jazz at the S
 weelinck Conservatory in Amsterdam. Now based near San Francisco\, he has 
 performed internationally with artists including Mathilde Santing\, Fapy L
 afertin\, Jimmy Rosenberg\, Stephane Wrembel\, and John Jorgenson\, and is
  a fixture on the Djangofest circuit.
LOCATION:Occidental
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/voyage-hot-
 club
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Storytelling with Brian Martens: The Story of Iron John
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270124T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270124T160000
UID:6b00dd1e3b7b1b40aeb1eee6@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Storytelling afternoon with Brian Martens: The Story of Iron J
 ohn.\nJoin Brian for a storytelling event designed to help you become the 
 author of your own myth and understand your place in the world. Iron John\
 , a Grimm Bros. tale\, is about the maturing of a young Prince who goes th
 rough initiations with curiosity and trust in a Wild Man. Each step on his
  path is a test\, an opening\, and an unknowing that leads him further int
 o maturity. The surprise ending matches the mystery\, revelation\, and myt
 hic consequences that an ancient tale reveals. There will be two short bre
 aks for discussion\, and a final Q&A. Refreshments will be available for s
 ale.\nPre-registration is suggested but not necessary. $25 non-OCA members
 \, $20 OCA members.\nGet Tickets\nBrian\, an abstract Artist\, Poet\, Auth
 or\, Creativity Facilitator\, International Speaker\, Myth Maker\, CA Poet
 s in the Schools Instructor\, Podcaster\, and Storyteller\, weaves poetry\
 , myth\, and reflection into all his storytelling. His first book\,\nThree
  Raven Gate\n\, is a collection of haiku\, the form he learned from his wo
 rk with Angeles Arrien Ph.D.\, a cross-cultural anthropologist\, over the 
 course of seven years. Brian seeks to inspire and motivate people\, with a
 rticles\, podcasts\, creativity workshops\, and poetry to recognize their 
 own deep creative spirit and to express that to the world.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/storytellin
 g-with-brian-martens-the-story-of-iron-john
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
